 (313, 336, 1510)]\\n\\nThe relationships indicate that dynamic recovery is part of dynamic restoration and is associated with strains below the level corresponding to peak flow stress. [Data: Relationships (309, 313, 336)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Dynamic recrystallization occurs in the post-peak steady-state region\",\"explanation\":\"Dynamic recrystallization is described as a restoration process that occurs during ongoing high-temperature deformation, particularly in the austenitic state and within the steady-state region. The flow-stress response falls from its maximum toward a stable level, and dynamic recrystallization is associated with this post-peak portion of deformation. [Data: Entities (253, 320, 282); Relationships (381, 316)]\\n\\nThe available evidence also connects dynamic recrystallization with refinement of α-grains in Nb-free steel, although the onset of the process is constrained by the large critical strain required to reach steady state. [Data: Entities (253, 327, 319); Relationships (389, 380)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Flow stress provides the process-response framework\",\"explanation\":\"During high-temperature austenitic deformation, flow stress initially increases with deformation, reaches peak stress, and then decreases toward a steady-state level. This response reflects the balance between work hardening and softening processes such as dynamic recrystallization. [Data: Entities (267, 258, 281); Relationships (302, 315)]\\n\\nThe data further state that the reciprocal of dynamically recrystallized grain size is proportional to flow stress and to the logarithm of the Zener–Hollomon parameter, linking the mechanical response to microstructural refinement. [Data: Entities (267)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Large critical strain limits dynamic-recrystallization grain refinement\",\"explanation\":\"Dynamic-recrystallization grain refinement is explicitly characterized as a refinement route associated with dynamic recrystallization. The evidence states that this route is almost impossible because the critical strain required for the onset of steady state is very large, even at high temperatures. [Data: Entities (327, 319); Relationships (389, 380)]\\n\\nThis constraint distinguishes dynamic recrystallization from dynamic recovery, which operates at lower strains and is directly associated with formation of a fine polygonal substructure. [Data: Entities (275, 1070); Relationships (313, 1510)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Restoration mechanisms remain coupled to subsequent structural change\",\"explanation\":\"Dynamic restoration includes both dynamic recovery and dynamic recrystallization as thermally activated processes during hot deformation. The structures produced by dynamic restoration are described as thermodynamically unstable and subject to modification by static restoration during subsequent holding at temperature. [Data: Entities (291); Relationships (305, 309)]\\n\\nThe community therefore represents a sequence in which deformation conditions, strain level, flow-stress evolution, and later thermal holding can all influence the resulting microstructure. The evidence specifically relates the softening mechanisms to hot working and describes their dependence on strain. [Data: Entities (274, 291); Relationships (308)]\"}],\"rating\":6.0,\"rating_explanation\":\"The community has moderate-to-high technical importance because it links steel processing conditions, flow-stress behavior, restoration mechanisms, and grain refinement, but the data provide no evidence of broader societal, legal, or operational impacts.\"}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1790706735, "model": "gpt-5.6-luna", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": "default", "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1090, "prompt_tokens": 3359, "total_tokens